%% Retrieving existing preshared key, bearer token or proof-of-possession credential
sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Attester
    participant CP as CAS Client Proxy
    participant PL as Platform Plugin
    participant SP as CAS Server Proxy
    participant CAC as Credential<br/>Acquisition<br/>Client
    participant CAS as Credential<br/>Acquisition<br/>Server

    autonumber

    note over A, CP: Client Proxy Call
    A->>CP: Obtain Credential<br/>(Context handle,<br/>Credential Type)
    activate CP
    CP->>CP: Validate Context handle,<br/>Map to Target
    note over CP, PL: Platform Plug-in Call
    CP->>PL: Prepare Key and Evidence<br/>for Credential Retrieval
    activate PL
    PL->>PL: Generate CWK
    PL->>PL: Generate Evidence with CWKpub
    PL-->>CP: Return CWK, Evidence
    deactivate PL
    note over CP, SP: CAS Proxy Call
    CP->>SP: Obtain Credential<br/>(Target, Evidence, Credential Type)
    deactivate CP
    activate SP
    SP->>SP: Pick Credential Acquisition Client<br/> based on Target
    note over SP, CAC: Server Proxy Call
    SP->>CAC: Obtain Credential<br/>(target, Evidence,<br/>Credential Type)
    deactivate SP
    activate CAC
    CAC->>CAC: Check Supported Credential Types,<br/>Reject on Mismatch
    CAC->>CAC: Encode the Request<br/>in the CAS Protocol Format
    note over CAC, CAS: CAS Protocol Call
    CAC->>CAS: Retrieve Credential<br/>(Evidence)
    deactivate CAC
    activate CAS
    CAS->>CAS: Process Retrieval Request<br/>by Contacting Verifier and<br/>Key/Credential Store
    CAS->>CAS: Encode the Response<br/>in the CAS Protocol Format
    CAS-->>CAC: Return the Wrapped Credential
    deactivate CAS
    activate CAC
    CAC->>CAC: Decode the Wrapped<br/>Credential Response
    CAC-->>CP: Return the Wrapped Credential
    deactivate CAC
    activate CP
    CP->>CP: Decrypt the Wrapped Credential<br/>using CWKpri
    CP-->>A: Return the<br/>Plaintext Credential
    deactivate CP